Description: Add enable_cef to chrome_grit_defines for preprocess_if_expr
 The build_webui.gni template uses chrome_grit_defines for preprocessor_defines
 when running preprocess_if_expr.py on TypeScript/HTML files. CEF's about_version.ts
 uses <if expr="enable_cef"> conditionals, so enable_cef must be in this list.
 .
 Note: chrome/common/features.gni already imports //cef/libcef/features/features.gni
 (added by CEF's patch_add_cef_to_features_gni.patch), which defines enable_cef.
 This patch only adds it to the chrome_grit_defines list for WebUI preprocessing.
 .
 Related patch 0028 handles a similar issue for components_strings GRIT target.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <juan.mendezr@proton.me>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-12-02

diff --git a/chrome/common/features.gni b/chrome/common/features.gni
index c46c6f6..425d9d2 100644
--- a/chrome/common/features.gni
+++ b/chrome/common/features.gni
@@ -105,4 +105,5 @@ chrome_grit_defines = [
   "optimize_webui=$optimize_webui",
   "chrome_root_store_cert_management_ui=$chrome_root_store_cert_management_ui",
   "use_nss_certs=$use_nss_certs",
+  "enable_cef=$enable_cef",
 ]
